YouCoded Android Application License
====================================

The YouCoded Android application — the source code in this `app/` directory
and the compiled Android Package (.apk / .aab) built from it — is licensed
under the MIT License, the full text of which follows below. This is the same
license as the rest of the YouCoded repository (see `../LICENSE`).

Third-party notice
------------------

The Android app includes a vendored copy of the Termux project's
terminal-emulator library (`../terminal-emulator-vendored/`, from
github.com/termux/termux-app tag v0.118.1, which in turn derives from
jackpal/Android-Terminal-Emulator). That library is licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0 — NOT GPLv3. Termux's own LICENSE.md carves the
terminal-emulator library out of the GPLv3 that covers the rest of the Termux
app. See `../terminal-emulator-vendored/LICENSE` for the Apache 2.0 text and
`../terminal-emulator-vendored/NOTICE` for the preserved copyright notices.

The Apache License 2.0 requires that NOTICE file to accompany any
redistribution of the library, in source or binary form. If you redistribute
the YouCoded Android app or a build of it, keep that NOTICE with it.

Termux packages (.deb) that the app downloads at runtime are separate programs
run as subprocesses; they are not part of this software and carry their own
licenses.

